## Sources and further reading {#sec-sources}

The terms used in section 2 come from @Rubin1976InferenceMissingData, and @Little1992RegressionMissingXs reviews the methods for regression with missing covariates, while @Allison2009MissingData offers a short, clear introduction to listwise deletion, to the methods that replace a missing value with a guess, and to maximum likelihood and multiple imputation. The case for the missing-indicator method in randomised experiments, and against complete cases there, is made by @ZhaoDing2024AdjustNotAdjust, under assumptions about nothing but the random assignment. Multiple imputation in political science is presented by @KingEtAl2001AnalyzingIncompletePolitical, and the mice package is described by its authors [@BuurenGroothuis-Oudshoorn2011MiceMultivariateImputation]. The construction of the analysis file, together with the checks on its missing values, is documented in the [module on building the analysis file](data-management.qmd), and the counts for every column are given in the [codebook of the analysis file](../data/housing_emails_codebook.md).
